      "refs": [
        "action:i1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start the process, begin by adding the image description and uploading the image."
      ],
      "justification": "The init marks the process trigger described in the opening unit, and the action paraphrases the required initial step without changing behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the message \"Image upload successful\" appears, then the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "The XOR branch splits on the upload result. The guard uses an abstract variable to capture the successful condition, routing to the success completion action and terminal node. Decision logic and outcome are preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the message indicates an unsuccessful upload, then try again."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard captures the unsuccessful path, and the action models the retry prompt. This faithfully represents the branching logic for failed uploads."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the option to try again is selected, the process will continue."
      ],
      "justification": "The second branch handles the retry choice. The guard captures the positive selection, converging back to restart the workflow, which correctly models continuing the process."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the option to try again is not selected, then an error will occur and the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the negative retry choice, triggering the error termination step and ending the process exactly as specified."
    }
  ],
